## Context
After PR #179 (frontier bench), the repo has 8 model YAML files with
duplicated entries across them. The same model (prices, context window,
params, reasoning flag) is copy-pasted into multiple files. When a field
changes, subsets drift out of sync — the missing `reasoning: true` on
DeepSeek R1 0528 in `models_frontier_10labs.yaml` was a concrete example.

## Actions
1. Merge all model definitions into a single `experiments/models.yaml`
   registry with tags/labels (e.g. `country`, `size_class`, `sweep` list).
2. Have sweep scripts select models by filter rather than by separate YAML
   files (e.g. `--filter country=CN` or a sweep config that references
   model IDs).
3. Remove the per-sweep/per-geography YAML files.

## Test
- All existing sweeps produce identical model lists from filtered registry.
- `pytest` passes with no regressions.

## Exit criteria
Single source of truth for model metadata. No duplicated model entries.
